    return agent(`${CONTEXT}\n\nYou are an ADVERSARIAL VERIFIER for the "${d.key}" review of this game. For EACH proposal below, independently check:\n1. Is the stated problem real? Verify in the code (open the cited lines) and, where it is about behavior or visuals, in the live game via a Playwright script. Reviewers often miss features that already exist in this large codebase — search app.js/model.js/README for it before accepting.\n2. Is the proposed change sound: correct mechanism, respects save compatibility, determinism, DOM-free model, existing tests, performance and the design language?\n3. Is the impact/effort estimate honest?\nVerdict: keep (correct as is), revise (real problem but proposal needs correction — give the corrected precise spec), reject (not real, already exists, harmful, or not worth it). For keep/revise, write revisedProposal as a precise implementation spec that an engineer could follow: exact functions/files, behavior, edge cases, and which tests to add. Default to reject when you cannot confirm the problem.\n\nScratch dir: ${SP}/verify/${d.key}/\n\nREVIEW SUMMARY:\n${review.summary}\n\nPROPOSALS:\n${JSON.stringify(review.proposals, null, 1)}`, { label: `verify:${d.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICTS })
