content.text:
Implementation is running again. The machine restarted overnight and stopped the previous run partway.

**Where things stand:** 13 of the 50 items are already committed on `transport-playability`.
- **Batch 1 (5 items):**
  - Notifications are never dropped; welcome, new-year and first-delivery moments get toasts, plus a News log.
  - Autosave no longer freezes vehicles, and a failed save is announced.
  - Right-click and Escape cancel a road drag.
  - Phones can't get stuck zoomed in.
  - Working freight routes are no longer mislabelled "No producer".
- **Batch 2 (8 items):**
  - Truthful all-or-nothing road building.
  - The "Next goal" card.
  - The route form picks cargo from the chosen stops.
  - A stable inspector panel.
  - Sentence-case labels.
  - "Continue" on the start menu and a paused chip.
  - Income floaters.
  - The render-cache fix for daily plant growth.

The batch-2 integration check was cut off by the restart while two browser checks were failing: the income-floater bunching test and one route-planner check. The new run fixes those first.

**What the new run does:**
1. Finishes batch 2: fixes those two checks, runs the full test suite and a quick play-through in the browser.
2. Implements the remaining 37 items in 6 more batches:
   - add or sell vehicles on a route;
   - drags that follow the terrain;
   - route highlighting;
   - milestones, town needs and route forecasts;
   - undo;
   - clickable vehicles;
   - contracts;
   - route editing and renaming;
   - a company report with a credit line;
   - status markers on industries;
   - towns building their own streets;
   - the mobile pass;
   - the performance follow-ups.

   I also added one item: fixing several older browser checks that time out at startup because they predate the start menu. We need those working to verify the release.
3. A final review with five angles: simulation and saves, UI code, a desktop play-test, whether the stacked features clutter the map, and phone use plus a performance comparison with the original.
4. A fix pass on whatever the review confirms, then a full sweep of every node test and browser check.

When that is green I'll fetch `origin`, check whether `main` has moved, fast-forward `main` to the branch and push. That deploys the live site.

The restart also wiped the scratch folder. I rebuilt all 51 specs from the saved review results, so nothing was lost. This will run for several hours; I'm checking in hourly.

